WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.650
Most people picture a pilgrim
heading for a holy site:

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:07.560
a saint's tomb, or a place
where someone reported a vision.

3
00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:11.560
But some Christians make their
journey to a living community instead,

4
00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:14.800
where people share prayer, work and meals.

5
00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:17.460
Guests cook, clean and wash up.

6
00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:20.360
They sing and pray together every day.

7
00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:22.080
Then they go home.

8
00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:27.000
So can a pilgrimage have no
shrine, no relic and no miracle?

9
00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:31.380
In this mission, you'll read what Jesus
said would mark out his followers.

10
00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:36.530
Then you'll weigh up whether a week in a
community beats a visit to a holy site.

11
00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:41.870
Your mission: find out whether a journey
with no shrine can still be a pilgrimage.
